        "verbs-irregular#to be born",
        "verbs-irregular#to die",
        "verbs#to return, to go back"
      ],
      "learn": [
        {
          "title": "être instead of avoir",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "About fifteen verbs form the passé composé with *être*, not *avoir*. Most of them are about moving from one place to another or a change: to go, to come, to arrive, to leave, to go in, to go out, to go up, to go down, to be born, to die, to stay, to fall, to come back."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "rows": [
                [
                  "aller",
                  "allé",
                  "Je suis allé à Nice."
                ],
                [
                  "venir",
                  "venu",
                  "Il est venu hier."
                ],
                [
                  "arriver",
                  "arrivé",
                  "Nous sommes arrivés à midi."
                ],
                [
                  "partir",
                  "parti",
                  "Tu es parti tôt."
                ],
                [
                  "entrer",
                  "entré",
                  "Je suis entré dans la salle."
                ],
                [
                  "sortir",
                  "sorti",
                  "Elle est sortie avec Paul."
                ],
                [
                  "monter",
                  "monté",
                  "Je suis monté au sommet."
                ],
                [
                  "descendre",
                  "descendu",
                  "On est descendus à la plage."
                ],
                [
                  "naître",
                  "né",
                  "Je suis né en 2000."
                ],
                [
                  "mourir",
                  "mort",
                  "Il est mort en 1900."
                ],
                [
                  "rester",
                  "resté",
                  "Je suis resté à la maison."
                ],
                [
                  "tomber",
                  "tombé",
                  "Il est tombé."
                ],
                [
                  "rentrer",
                  "rentré",
                  "Je suis rentré à six heures."
                ],
                [
                  "devenir",
                  "devenu",
                  "Il est devenu médecin."
                ]
              ],
              "textCols": [],
              "head": [
                "verb",
                "participle",
                "example"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "Hier, je ___ allé au cinéma.",
                "a": [
                  "suis"
                ],
                "hint": "être"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Memory aid: the house",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "verb": "aller",
              "tense": "passe-compose"
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "title": "house",
              "en": "Picture a house. You *entrer* (go in) and *sortir* (go out), go up and down the stairs (*monter, descendre*), *arriver* at the house and *partir* from it, *rester* in it, *tomber* out of the window. What happens around the house takes *être*."
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "We arrived on Monday.",
                "a": [
                  "Nous sommes {arrivés|arrivées} lundi.",
                  "On est {arrivés|arrivées} lundi."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "vocab"
            }
          ]
        }
